The NA62 experiment at CERN has recently published a study on the rare kepleran decay $K^+ 	o \pi^+ 
u  ar{
u}$ using data collected in 2016. This research focused on analyzing a massive dataset of $K^+ 	o \pi^+ 
u  ar{
u}$ decays and $K^+ 	o \pi^0 e^+ 
eutrino$ decays, resulting in significantly enhanced sensitivity. With a significantly improved single event sensitivity of $10^{-10}$, this study represents a notable advancement over the previous best limit of $10^{-9}$ set by the CLEO collaboration.
